The board of commissioners of the county shall continue to be the chief executive entity of the county, and it shall be the duty of the board to set the overall executive policies and procedures of the county. The manager shall be the chief administrative officer of the county, fully responsible to the chairman and other members of the board for the proper and efficient administration of all the affairs of the county, including all of the day to day operations of the county except as otherwise provided by law. Specifically, it shall be the duty of the manager:
(1) To appoint and remove all department heads in the administrative service of Douglas County government with the express advice and consent of the board, as provided for by this article and in compliance with the Douglas County merit system or personnel rules adopted by the county, except the county attorney and county clerk; who shall be appointed and removed only by the board;
(2) To supervise the administration of all departments, offices and agencies of the county or any that may be created except as otherwise provided by law or ordinance with the advice of the board;
(3) To submit to the board the annual operating budget for the county, specifically including a capital improvement budget, which has been prepared by the budget/fiance officer. Also, the manager shall obtain from all department heads and local constitutional officers their proposed annual budgets;
(4) To submit to the board and make available to the public a complete report on the finances and administrative activities of the county as of the end of each fiscal year and at such other times as the board may direct;
(5) To prepare and make such other reports concerning the operations of departments, offices and agencies of the government as may be required by the board;
(6) To keep all commissioners fully advised as to the financial condition and needs of the county and make such recommendations to the board concerning the affairs of the county as he deems desirable;
(7) To confer with and assist the directors of all departments, such as the department of health and department of family and children services, whose responsibilities and activities are not under direct control and jurisdiction of the commissioners, but who are dependent upon appropriations therefrom, and provide general liaison between the commissioners and all departments, boards, commissions and employees of the county;
(8) To confer with and advise all elected and appointed officials of the government who are not under the immediate control or jurisdiction of the commissioners, but who receive financial support therefrom, including but not limited to the clerk of the superior court, judge of the probate court, sheriff and tax commissioner;
(9) To examine regularly accounts, records and operations of every board, commission, authority, department, office and agency which receive appropriations from the Commissioners;
(10) To see that the ordinances, resolutions and regulations of the board and the laws of the state are forth fully executed and enforced;
(11) The manager shall not engage in or be concerned with local partisan politics or any local political campaign. He shall not contribute to any local campaign fund or solicit funds for local political purposes from any other person. He shall not be eligible for election as a member of the board of commissioners of Douglas County for a period of one (1) year after termination of his service as county manager.
(Res. of 3-2-93)

